From: VeraOS image qualification <veraos@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] fdo: ignore bufferless surface commits before SHM export

A Wayland surface commit without an attached wl_buffer must not forward
the previous surface.shmBuffer pointer (or dmabuf) after bufferResource
has been cleared by the prior commit. That stale pointer produced
nonphysical SHM width/height/stride in Cog's export callback and a
source-buffer fault. Preserve normal exports when bufferResource exists.

Upstream WPEBackend-FDO 1.14.3 patch candidate, not a claim that
runtime refresh is qualified.

--- a/src/ws-egl.cpp
+++ b/src/ws-egl.cpp
@@ -83,8 +83,12 @@
         return;
 
     struct wl_resource* bufferResource = surface.bufferResource;
     surface.bufferResource = nullptr;
+
+    // A commit without a new wl_buffer must not re-export stale SHM data.
+    if (!bufferResource)
+        return;
 
     if (surface.dmabufBuffer)
         surface.apiClient->exportLinuxDmabuf(surface.dmabufBuffer);
     else if (surface.shmBuffer)
--- a/src/ws-shm.cpp
+++ b/src/ws-shm.cpp
@@ -46,8 +46,12 @@
 
     struct wl_resource* bufferResource = surface.bufferResource;
     surface.bufferResource = nullptr;
 
+    // A commit without a new wl_buffer must not re-export stale SHM data.
+    if (!bufferResource)
+        return;
+
     if (surface.shmBuffer)
         surface.apiClient->exportShmBuffer(bufferResource, surface.shmBuffer);
     else
         surface.apiClient->exportBufferResource(bufferResource);
